# Local pN fixtures (boundary)

## Hard split

| Fixture | Who | When |
|---|---|---|
| `.local/test-pn/` | **User** | Your QA identity. You run it yourself. |
| `.local/cursor-test-pn/` | Fixtures only | Used only when **you** explicitly ask to run dual-pN or fixture harness scripts — not for agent browser QA. |

The agent **never** opens, unlocks, or uploads `.local/test-pn/`.

**There is no third fixture.** Do not create `.local/test-pn-2` again. Dual-pN B is `cursor-test-pn` when a harness needs two identities.

## Agent rules

1. Do not commit `.local/`, log Key 1/Key 2 / passcode / pn name, or paste secrets into git, PRs, or plan files.
2. Do not create, mint, or live-create identities unless the user explicitly asks for that workflow.
3. Dual-pN / fixture scripts may load `test-pn` + `cursor-test-pn` only when the user explicitly asks. Still follow `agent-scope.mdc` (no browser MCP unless the user requests it in that chat).
4. Crypto and auth acceptance stays on hermetic package tests.
